---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site, fullAddress } from '@/config/site';
import { pages } from '@/data/pages';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy policy', path: '/privacy' },
];
---

<LegalLayout {...pages.privacy} heading="Privacy policy" updated="2026-10-13" crumbs={crumbs}>
  <p>
    This policy explains how {site.legalName} (“Akrostech”, “we”, “us”) collects, uses and protects personal information when you visit
    {site.url.replace('https://', '')} or contact us. It does not cover the data we process on behalf of clients under a services agreement; that
    is governed by the agreement and its data-protection terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>{site.legalName}, {fullAddress}. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or call {site.phone} with any privacy question.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <p>
    When you send an enquiry, we collect your name, work email, and, if you choose to give them, your company, phone number, the service you are
    interested in, your team size and your message. When you book a call through Calendly, Calendly collects the details you enter under its own
    privacy policy and shares them with us.
  </p>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider records standard server logs (IP address, browser type, pages requested and timestamps) to keep the site secure and
    working. We do not use advertising cookies or sell personal information. The site stores two preferences in your browser: your light or dark
    theme choice and whether you have seen the opening animation in this session. These never leave your device.
  </p>
  <h3>Embedded content</h3>
  <p>
    Our contact and location pages embed Google Maps, which may set cookies and collect data under Google’s privacy policy when the map loads.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to your enquiry and arrange a discovery call.</li>
    <li>To prepare a proposal and, if you become a client, to deliver our services.</li>
    <li>To keep the website secure, prevent spam and fix problems.</li>
    <li>To meet legal, accounting and tax obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We rely on your consent (which you give when you submit the form and can withdraw at any time), our legitimate interest in responding to
    business enquiries and running our website, and, for clients, the performance of our contract.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share personal information only with service providers who help us run our business, under contracts that require them to protect it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>our website host (Vercel) and email delivery provider (Resend);</li>
    <li>our scheduling provider (Calendly), if you book a call;</li>
    <li>our professional advisers, where needed;</li>
    <li>authorities, where the law requires it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Some providers process data outside your state or country. Where required, we use appropriate safeguards for those transfers.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries that do not lead to an engagement are deleted within 24 months of our last contact. Client records are kept for the life of the
    engagement and as long afterwards as tax and legal obligations require. Server logs are kept for up to 90 days.
  </p>

  <h2>How we protect it</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served only over HTTPS. Access to enquiry data is limited to the staff who need it, with named accounts and multi-factor
    authentication. Our team members sign confidentiality agreements.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights and choices</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, including under the California Consumer Privacy Act and similar state laws, you may have the right to know what
    personal information we hold about you, to correct or delete it, to obtain a copy, and to opt out of its sale or sharing for targeted
    advertising. We do not sell or share personal information for advertising. To exercise any right, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}
      >{site.email}</a
    >. We will verify your request and respond within the time the law requires, and we will not treat you differently for exercising your
    rights.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Our website and services are for businesses. We do not knowingly collect information from children under 16.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top of this page. Significant changes will be highlighted on the site.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or requests: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, {site.phone}, or by post to {site.legalName}, {fullAddress}.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
